---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';
import record from '../../samples/criterion-record.json.txt?raw';

const toc = [
   { id: 'sources', label: 'Where the data comes from' },
   { id: 'record', label: 'A criterion record' },
   { id: 'files', label: 'The data files' },
   { id: 'license', label: 'W3C text and its license' },
   { id: 'refresh', label: 'Refresh the data' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="WCAG data"
   summary="<p>a11ied ships WCAG 2.1 and 2.2 inside the package: every criterion, its techniques, the W3C's guidance, and how to test it. Lookups read those files, so they work offline and return the same answer every time.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="sources">Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p>a11ied pins these sources and merges them into one record per criterion.</p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>W3C WCAG 2.1 and 2.2</dt>
         <dd>Criterion numbers, titles, levels, the normative text, techniques, and failures.</dd>
         <dt>W3C Understanding documents</dt>
         <dd>The W3C's explanation of each criterion.</dd>
         <dt>W3C ACT rules</dt>
         <dd>Which test rule covers which criterion.</dd>
         <dt>W3C quick reference tags</dt>
         <dd>Topic tags per criterion, which <a href="/relevant-criteria">relevance</a> matches against.</dd>
         <dt>axe-core</dt>
         <dd>Rule IDs and the criteria each rule is tagged with, read from the installed package.</dd>
         <dt>W3C ARIA Authoring Practices Guide</dt>
         <dd>The patterns and examples <code>a1 pattern</code> prints.</dd>
         <dt>WCAG2Mobile</dt>
         <dd>The W3C task force's guidance on applying WCAG to mobile apps. It is an Editor's Draft, not a W3C Recommendation.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="record">A criterion record</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 wcag show 1.4.3 --json</code></pre>
      <pre data-label="OUTPUT"><code>{record.trimEnd()}</code></pre>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>criterion</code></dt>
         <dd>The requirement. Beyond what is shown: <code>normativeText</code> as HTML, <code>details</code> for the exceptions, and <code>techniques</code>, <code>advisoryTechniques</code>, and <code>failures</code>, each with an <code>id</code>, <code>title</code>, and <code>url</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>versions</code></dt>
         <dd>The WCAG releases that contain the criterion.</dd>
         <dt><code>testMethod</code>, <code>strategy</code></dt>
         <dd>How the criterion has to be tested. See <a href="/test-methods">test methods</a>.</dd>
         <dt><code>mobileGuidance</code></dt>
         <dd>What WCAG2Mobile says about the criterion. It covers Levels A and AA. An entry whose <code>state</code> is <code>placeholder</code> has not been written by the task force yet.</dd>
         <dt><code>understandingExcerpt</code></dt>
         <dd>The opening of the Understanding document. <code>a1 wcag understanding 1.4.3</code> prints all of it.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="files">The data files</h2>
      <p>
         The files are in the <code>@a11ied/wcag-data</code> package, one set per WCAG
         version. Use the <a href="/reference/api#wcag">API</a> or the CLI to read them. The
         file layout can change between releases.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>criteria</code>, <code>criteria-by-level</code>, <code>slug-index</code></dt>
         <dd>The criterion records, and indexes by level and by slug.</dd>
         <dt><code>test-methods</code>, <code>test-method-summary</code>, <code>strategy</code></dt>
         <dd>The test method of each criterion, the counts per level, and the testing strategy.</dd>
         <dt><code>technique-index</code>, <code>failure-index</code>, <code>technique-bodies</code></dt>
         <dd>Techniques and failures: their titles, the criteria that list them, and their text.</dd>
         <dt><code>axe-rules</code>, <code>act-rules</code></dt>
         <dd>Each rule and the criteria it maps to.</dd>
         <dt><code>understanding</code>, <code>documents-content</code></dt>
         <dd>The Understanding documents, converted to Markdown.</dd>
         <dt><code>apg-patterns</code>, <code>mobile-guidance</code></dt>
         <dd>The ARIA patterns and the mobile guidance. One file each, for both versions.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="license">W3C text and its license</h2>
      <p>
         The Understanding documents and technique pages are W3C text, converted from HTML to
         Markdown under the W3C Document License. The package includes a
         <code>NOTICE.md</code> with the attribution. Every command that prints this text
         also prints the title and URL of the document it came from.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="refresh">Refresh the data</h2>
      <p>
         This is for maintainers. Nothing in normal use fetches data. From the repository
         root:
      </p>
      <pre><code>npm run wcag:sync
npm run wcag:validate</code></pre>
      <p>
         <code>wcag:sync</code> downloads the sources and regenerates the files.
         <code>wcag:validate</code> checks them against the recorded sources. Review the diff
         before you commit it.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
